{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 170,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You may have heard that Einstein's theory\nof special relativity imposes a cosmic speed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3850,
    "dDurationMs": 4950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "limit: nothing can travel faster than the\nspeed of light. Well, that's wrong. All that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8800,
    "dDurationMs": 3589,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Einstein said was that light moves at the\nsame speed in every reference frame - and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12389,
    "dDurationMs": 3881,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "while this implies that nothing with real\nmass can move faster than light, it doesn't"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16270,
    "dDurationMs": 1470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "impose a cosmic speed limit."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17740,
    "dDurationMs": 3350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because you can break the speed of light in\nyour backyard. All you have to do is point"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21090,
    "dDurationMs": 4010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a laser beam at the moon and flick your wrist.\nThe spot of light from the laser beam will"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25100,
    "dDurationMs": 3330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "travel across the moon's face in about half\na millisecond, which means it's traveling"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28430,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at twenty times the speed of light!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30410,
    "dDurationMs": 3739,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How is this possible? Well, think about a\ncomputer screen – what's the speed limit"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34149,
    "dDurationMs": 4050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for pixels on the screen? Zero. Pixels can't\nmove."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38199,
    "dDurationMs": 3230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if you cleverly arrange a whole bunch\nof pixels to turn on and off in a special"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41429,
    "dDurationMs": 3331,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "way, you can make an image that appears to\nmove across the screen, even though every"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44760,
    "dDurationMs": 3599,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pixel stays put. So you've broken the speed\nof pixels!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48359,
    "dDurationMs": 3710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The laser pointer on the moon is basically\nthe same - each photon travels to the moon"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52069,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at the speed of light, but the image of a\ndot that they form on the surface moves twenty"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 55819,
    "dDurationMs": 4580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "times faster! No physical laws are broken\nbecause nothing physical is actually traveling"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60399,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "faster than light - it's just an image."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63069,
    "dDurationMs": 3931,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And as you may have guessed, the red dot of\na laser is pretty big by the time it gets"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67000,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the moon – depending on your laser, it\nmight be five hundred or a thousand kilometers"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70960,
    "dDurationMs": 7000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "across! So don't worry about blinding any\nastronauts."
    } ]
  } ]
}
